Arara Code: generic theme-color attention hook for native view container icons.

Why a patch: WebviewView.badge (stable) and the available proposed APIs only
provide numeric badges, not the foreground or running shine of a native
composite-bar icon/label. The extension owns completion/unread/running state
and supplies a theme color id or `{ shine: true }` through
_workbench.setViewContainerAttention(containerId, colorId | { shine: true } | undefined).
The core only stores/renders this presentation override. No provider names or
product rules live here; selection and theme changes retain the native behavior.
Touches: src/vs/workbench/browser/parts/compositeBarActions.ts, src/vs/workbench/browser/parts/media/paneCompositePart.css

